---@class posthog.event_definitions.ListEventDefinitionsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field event_type? posthog.event_definitions.ListEventDefinitionsRequestEventType|string `event_custom` keeps only names without a `$` prefix and `event_posthog` only names with one. Default `event`.
---@field exclude_hidden? boolean When true, omit events that have been explicitly hidden by a team admin (Enterprise only).
---@field exclude_stale? boolean When true, omit events whose last ingested occurrence is older than 30 days. Events that have never been seen (`last_seen_at` is null) are kept so newly-defined events remain discoverable. Default false. If a search returns zero results with this filter on, retry with `exclude_stale=false` and tell the user the matches are stale.
---@field excluded_properties? string JSON-encoded list of event names to omit. The name matches the property definitions endpoint that shares it.
---@field fuzzy_search? boolean When true, find similar event names only if the filtered search has no matches.
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field names? posthog.event_definitions.ListEventDefinitionsRequestNamesList Return exact matches for these event names. Pass names as repeated or comma-separated values.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field ordering? posthog.event_definitions.ListEventDefinitionsRequestOrderingList Sort keys, prefixed with `-` for descending. Default `-last_seen_at::date` then `name`. Projects with more than 100000 event definitions default to `name`, unless the request sets `search`, `exclude_stale`, `verified`, `names`, `tags` or `event_type=event_posthog`.
---@field search? string Case-insensitive match on the event name. Every whitespace-separated term has to match.
---@field tags? string JSON-encoded list of tag names. Keeps events that carry any of them.
---@field verified? boolean When true, keep only verified events and core PostHog events. When false, keep the rest (Enterprise only).

